{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794652558,"nonce":"Ct/W2/0uVfa9ReBMIWajB3PyqRA=","title":"xwindow, xavi and xgpu through hxn, generated by x-idl","message":"xwindow, xavi and xgpu each declare their API once (`api/*.api.rs`) and keep their operations in a backend shared by every runtime; x-idl generates a thin adapter per runtime. Decided with the user on 2026-11-14: x-idl gains an hxn target, which writes the library's binding as Rust marked for hxn, and hxn builds every runtime from it. The Haxe API each library has today stays, with hxn's classes where hxn has an equivalent (`hxn.Future` for `ash.Future`, `haxe.io.Bytes` for `XidlBytes`, an hxn class for a resource that is an `abstract (Int)` today). x-idl's own HashLink generator is retired once hxn has proven itself on these libraries. The generator lives in x-idl.\n\nHow the declaration maps (checked against hlwindow's generated `haxe/window`):\n\n- A resource (`trait Window`, `Box\u003cWindow\u003e`, `this: \u0026Window`) is an `#[hxn::interface]`; its methods call the backend function `#[native(...)]` names. Static methods are functions without a receiver.\n- A descriptor (`struct WindowAttributes`) is a native builder today: `new WindowAttributes()` and one setter a field. It stays one: an `#[hxn::interface]` with `new` and a `\u0026mut self` setter a field. A descriptor that holds a resource (xgpu's `BindingResource`, `AttachmentView`, the view arrays) takes it through a setter, which hxn already accepts, so hxn needs no objects inside data for this.\n- A C-like enum is an `#[hxn::data]` enum: `enum abstract X(Int)`, the same shape as today.\n- A tagged enum (xwindow's `Event`) is an `#[hxn::data]` tagged enum: a Haxe `enum`. hxn writes its argument names in camel case (`scaleFactor` for `scale_factor`); a `switch` binds arguments by position, so programs are unaffected.\n- x-idl's optional wrappers (`OptionalText`, `OptionalFloat`, ...) can be emitted as tagged enums, keeping their shape.\n- `Buffer` / `BufferMut` / `Text` are `\u0026[u8]` / `\u0026mut [u8]` / `\u0026str` and `String`; mapped GPU memory crosses as copies (`copyIn`, `copyOut`).\n- Every `Future\u003c...\u003e` in the three APIs carries a resource or `()`, which hxn carries.\n- xgpu makes a surface from raw window handles passed as `i64`, so nothing crosses between the two libraries.\n\nWhat hxn needs first:\n\n1. A Haxe package for a library's classes (`window`, `gpu`): today they are all in the top-level package.\n2. Source generated by a build script: `hxn build` parses the library before cargo runs, so it cannot see a module written to `OUT_DIR` and `include!`d. It would run the library's build script first, read `out_dir` from cargo's JSON messages, and follow the `include!`.\n3. Method names: x-idl's are camel case and would be emitted in snake case, which hxn turns back; any name that does not survive the round trip needs a way to name the Haxe method.\n\nOpen: Ash treats hlwindow specially on Android and iOS (a fiber under the host's loop on iOS, `xwindow_main` on Android); a library built by hxn has to be recognised the same way. `Option\u003cText\u003e` could also be `Null\u003cString\u003e`, as hxn has it, at the cost of programs that match `OptionalText.Some`.\n\nOrder: xwindow (115 functions, no resource inside a descriptor), xavi, xgpu.","files":null}]}